{"artifacts":[],"cancelled_at":null,"effects":[],"expected_sha":"21a180b6fc557f65436fc14bb6dafa1bdc57df8f","generation":2,"intent":{"claim":"b2f9fe9811d44b15bf179c30358a4606","dispatch_status":"acknowledged","id":"f4a17224e1a54f9188f2195ed498f702","recorded_at":1791521628},"iteration":1,"next_check_at":1791522296,"phase":"75b132153145437f916a64645a612689","publications":[],"reason":null,"report":null,"request":{"authorized_actor_id":218610,"baseline_review_ids":[5464843292,5465783898],"budgets":{"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udfe1 Changes recommended\n\nCAS retries can lose fallback state and permit another request from an exhausted fallback requester.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>2 open findings</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Persist merged fallback state across CAS retry failures](#discussion_r4226680419) \u00b7 New\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Low severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Document Copilot gate release behavior without fallback](#discussion_r4226680469) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n\ud83e\udde0 **Review effort:** Balanced","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5465783898","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5465783898},{"body":"The retry snapshot is merged only into the in-memory `fallbacks` mapping. After a CAS push failure, the next attempt can skip every request because the request receipt was also restored, so this mapping is never saved and the fallback record created by the failed attempt is lost. A later push can then treat all existing quota notices as the baseline and send another request from the already exhausted fallback requester. Persist the merged fallback state before any loop `continue` paths, and add a CAS-retry regression test.","comment_commit_id":"21a180b6fc557f65436fc14bb6dafa1bdc57df8f","comment_id":4226680419,"key":"inline:4226680419","kind":"inline","line":78,"original_commit_id":"21a180b6fc557f65436fc14bb6dafa1bdc57df8f","original_line":78,"path":".github/scripts/pull-request-dashboard/copilot_review_delivery.py","review_commit_id":"21a180b6fc557f65436fc14bb6dafa1bdc57df8f","review_id":5465783898,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-09T04:44:06Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"e8f324dffd677977805254b91edd867f17adebaf3354c66378a49a2e45fb700f","id":4226680419,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-09T04:44:06Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDOTENyc86qpcTr"},{"body":"The documented gate semantics no longer match the implementation. This still says a clean Copilot review is required and that a quota notice does not count as a review, but the new logic immediately releases the Copilot gate when no fallback token is configured (or after the fallback is exhausted), while retaining required-check and actionable-feedback blockers. Please document that release behavior, including the optional fallback case, so operators can predict when a PR routes without a completed review.","comment_commit_id":"21a180b6fc557f65436fc14bb6dafa1bdc57df8f","comment_id":4226680469,"key":"inline:4226680469","kind":"inline","line":142,"original_commit_id":"21a180b6fc557f65436fc14bb6dafa1bdc57df8f","original_line":142,"path":"pull-request-dashboard/README.md","review_commit_id":"21a180b6fc557f65436fc14bb6dafa1bdc57df8f","review_id":5465783898,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-09T04:44:06Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"836c043d151afd0f0dd227ef121c4c51402b9fdb1374edaede0c2ff2ae5e080e","id":4226680469,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-09T04:44:06Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDOTENyc86qpcUN"}],"frozen_at":1791521602,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-09T04:53:22Z","frozen_sha":"21a180b6fc557f65436fc14bb6dafa1bdc57df8f","head_ref":"trask-copilot-review-loop","head_repo":"open-telemetry/shared-workflows","head_repo_id":1279488627,"input_mode":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":37884850288},"loop_kind":"copilot_review","mode":"publish","pr":452,"protocol":"reviewable-v1","publication":{"auth_mode":"fine_grained_pat","authorized_actor_id":218610,"authorized_at":1791520741,"generation":2,"max_pipelines":5,"phase":"75b132153145437f916a64645a612689","profile":"reviewable-v1","required_checks":[]},"repo":"open-telemetry/shared-workflows","repo_id":1279488627,"request_id":"f4a17224e1a54f9188f2195ed498f702","schema":2,"source_private":false,"target_private":false,"workflow_ref":"review-loop-revisions/eadecd0ffce9590595791925dd85130dae808235","workflow_revision":"eadecd0ffce9590595791925dd85130dae808235"},"run":{"attempt":1,"conclusion":null,"id":37886022192,"url":"https://github.com/trask/copilot-workflows/actions/runs/37886022192"},"schema":2,"seen_findings":["c2f8fd163056601cdd4b0384d140e0a3fffde63585cd04952d18db559c7ff773"],"seen_inline_findings":["89b6523960ef06